Title: How to change the background color of a form?.
Body: <p>I'm not able to change the background color of a Form in SwiftUI for iOS &lt; 16. It always takes default form backgroundcolor depending on which color scheme is selected in the iPhone settings. All solution I found here to set the UITableView.appearance().backgroundColor = .clear also don't work. Do any of you have a solution?</p>
<p>I tried different solutions:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>UITableView.appearance().backgroundColor = .clear</p>
</li>
<li>
<pre><code>GeometryReader { geometry in
            ZStack {
                Rectangle().foregroundColor(.white).frame(width: geometry.size.width, height: geometry.size.height)
                Form {
                    // your form content here
                }
            }
        }
</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<pre><code>struct FormBackgroundColorModifier: ViewModifier {
    var color: Color

    func body(content: Content) -&gt; some View {
        ZStack {
            color.edgesIgnoringSafeArea(.all)
            content
        }
    }
}

struct MyForm: View {
    var body: some View {
        Form {

        }
        .modifier(FormBackgroundColorModifier(color: .white))
    }
}

</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>

Answers:
Here's a possible solution to change the background color of a form in SwiftUI for iOS &lt; 16:
<pre><code>struct FormBackgroundColorModifier: ViewModifier {
    var color: Color

    func body(content: Content) -&gt; some View {
        ZStack {
            color.edgesIgnoringSafeArea(.all)
            content
        }
    }
}

struct MyForm: View {
    var body: some View {
        Form {
            // your form content here
        }
        .modifier(FormBackgroundColorModifier(color: .white))
    }
}
</code></pre>
This code uses a view modifier to change the background color of a form. It creates a modifier that takes a color as input and returns a view with the background color set to that color. The modifier is then applied to the form using the .modifier() modifier.
This should work for iOS &lt; 16. If you're using iOS 16 or later, you can use the background() modifier instead:
<pre><code>struct MyForm: View {
    var body: some View {
        Form {
            // your form content here
        }
        .background(.white)
    }
}
</code></pre>
This code sets the background color of the form to white using the .background() modifier.
I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.

