Title: Cypress - Comparing element text within an array loop.
Body: <p>I have a page with card elements, and more cards are loaded as the user scrolls down. I am trying to write a test to scroll down until all the card elements are loaded.</p>
<p>What I am trying:</p>
<ol>
<li>Get the text of the last card on the page (lastCard)</li>
<li>Scroll down</li>
<li>Get the text of the last card that just loaded (currentCard)</li>
<li>If both cards have the same text, then end the loop. Repeat if not.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>let stopScroll
let currentCard
let lastCard
let scrollArray = Array.from({length:100},(v,k)=&gt;k+1)
    cy.wrap(scrollArray).each((index) =&gt; {
            if (stopScroll != true) {
                cy.get('[data-testid=&quot;card&quot;]').last().then(($element) =&gt; {
                    lastCard = $element.text();
                })
                cy.get('[data-testid=&quot;footer&quot;]').scrollIntoView().should('be.visible')
                cy.wait(1000)
                cy.get('[data-testid=&quot;card&quot;]').last().then(($element) =&gt; {
                    currentCard = $element.text();
                    if (lastCard == currentCard){
                        stopScroll = true
                        cy.log(stopScroll)
                        }
                })
                .then(() =&gt; {
                    if (stopScroll == true){
                    return false
                }
              })
            }
        })
</code></pre>
<p>The loop keeps going on even though stopScroll is being set to true.
Everything seems to work up to the point of &quot;.then(()&quot;. I am unsure whether this is the correct way to go about this.</p>

Answers:
To address your issue, you should use `cy.wait()` to ensure the element's text is updated after scrolling. Here's a revised version of your code:

<pre><code>let stopScroll
let currentCard
let lastCard
let scrollArray = Array.from({length:100},(v,k)=&gt;k+1)

cy.wrap(scrollArray).each((index) =&gt; {
  if (stopScroll != true) {
    cy.get('[data-testid="card"]').last().then(($element) =&gt; {
      lastCard = $element.text();
    })
    cy.get('[data-testid="footer"]').scrollIntoView().should('be.visible')
    cy.wait(1000) // Add a wait here to ensure the element is updated
    cy.get('[data-testid="card"]').last().then(($element) =&gt; {
      currentCard = $element.text();
      if (lastCard == currentCard) {
        stopScroll = true
        cy.log(stopScroll)
      }
    })
  }
})
</code></pre>

This change ensures that the Cypress command waits for the element's text to update after scrolling. Make sure to include `cy.wait(1000)` after the scroll action to ensure the element's text is updated. If you still encounter issues, you may need to adjust the wait time or use `cy.wait()` with a selector to wait for a specific element to appear.

If you're still having trouble, please provide more details about the behavior you're experiencing, such as any error messages or unexpected results.

