Answers:
To use the <strong>toSorted</strong> method in typescript, you need to import the <strong>Array</strong> class from the <strong>typescript</strong> library. Then, you can use the <strong>toSorted</strong> method on an array of numbers like this:</p>
<pre><code>import { Array } from 'typescript';

const x = [1, 2];
const y = Array.from(x).toSorted();
</code></pre>
<p>This will return a new array with the elements sorted in ascending order.</p>
<p>If you want to sort the array in descending order, you can use the <strong>toReverse</strong> method like this:</p>
<pre><code>import { Array } from 'typescript';

const x = [1, 2];
const y = Array.from(x).toReverse();
</code></pre>
<p>This will return a new array with the elements sorted in descending order.</p>
<p>If you want to remove elements from an array using the <strong>toSplice</strong> method, you can use it like this:</p>
<pre><code>import { Array } from 'typescript';

const x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const y = Array.from(x).toSplice(2, 2);
</code></pre>
<p>This will return a new array with the elements removed from index 2 to index 3.</p>
<p>I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.</p>
