Title: How do I convert the numbers in my Vector&lt;Object&gt; into int?.
Body: <p>How do I convert the numbers in my vector into int? I'm trying the numbers in my object array into int values for my if statenebt, but I can't find a way to do so. Can anyone help tell me what I would need to do?</p>
<pre><code>private static void test() {
    Vector&lt;Object&gt; vector = new Vector&lt;Object&gt;();
    vector.add(1);
        vector.add(2);
        vector.add(5);
        vector.add(6);
        System.out.println(&quot;\nThe Vector is: &quot; + vector);
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; vector.size(); i++)
        {      
          int d = vector.get(i);
          if(d%2 == 0) 
          {
              System.out.println(d);

          }
}
</code></pre>
<p>I tried using cast, i.e., <code>(int)</code>, but it didn't work. The result I want is to print out only the odd numbers in the vector.</p>

Answers:
None. Use the following code to convert the numbers in your Vector&lt;Object&gt; into int values:
<pre><code>private static void test() {
    Vector&lt;Object&gt; vector = new Vector&lt;Object&gt;();
    vector.add(1);
    vector.add(2);
    vector.add(5);
    vector.add(6);
    System.out.println(&quot;\nThe Vector is: &quot; + vector);
    for (int i = 0; i &lt; vector.size(); i++)
    {      
      int d = (int) vector.get(i);
      if(d%2 == 0) 
      {
          System.out.println(d);

      }
}
</code></pre>
The above code converts the numbers in your Vector&lt;Object&gt; into int values and prints out only the odd numbers in the vector. Note that you need to cast the Object to int before you can use it in your if statement. This will allow you to perform the modulo operation on the int value and print out only the odd numbers in the vector.
<|fim_suffix|><|fim_middle|>
