A map is used when you need to store a collection of key-value pairs, where the keys are unique identifiers and the values can be of any type. The keys can be of any data type, but the values must be of the same type.

On the other hand, a set is used when you need to store a collection of unique values, where the order of the values does not matter. A set is useful when you need to ensure that there are no duplicates in a collection of values.

Here's an example of how to define a map and a set in Python:

<pre><code># Map
