Title: Why copy constructor does not need to consider half-assignment in C++.
Body: <p>I've read about that to avoid copy assignment operator from doing half-assignment (it throws some exceptions when copying items so the target of assignment come to a state of mixed old and new value). The code below provides a solution</p>
<pre><code>Matrix&amp; Matrix::operator=(const Matrix&amp; m)
{
    Matrix tmp{m};
    swap(tmp, *this);  // only be called when copy succeeds
    return *this;
}
</code></pre>
