Title: Razor Page Unable to Call Service Method CS0120.
Body: <p>I am using the service ITADService with the following method:</p>
<pre><code>public async Task GetAllGames()
{
var result = InterpretStringResponse((await _http.GetAsync(&quot;api/itad&quot;)).ToString());
}
</code></pre>
<p>My razor page calls this method with:</p>
<pre><code>protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
{
    await ITADService.GetAllGames();    
}
</code></pre>
<p>This leads to the CS0120 build-time error stating that an object reference is necessary, yet when I create an instance of the service on the page with:</p>
<pre><code>private readonly HttpClient _http;
ITADService service = new ITADService(_http);
</code></pre>
<p>Visual Studio tells me that an initializer cannot reference it if it isn't static.</p>
<p>How is this supposed to be done? Is the error in the service or the page?</p>

Answers:
To resolve this error, you need to make sure that the `ITADService` instance is created and used within the context of an asynchronous method. In your case, since you are trying to call a method on `ITADService` from the `OnInitializedAsync` method of a Razor page, you should ensure that the service instance is properly initialized and used within an asynchronous context. Here's how you can do it:

1. **Ensure the Service Instance is Properly Initialized:**
   - Initialize the `ITADService` instance within an asynchronous method.
   - Use `await` to ensure that the service methods are called asynchronously.

2. **Use `ITADService` in an Asynchronous Method:**
   - Call the `GetAllGames` method within an asynchronous method, such as `OnInitializedAsync`.

Here's the updated code:

```csharp
// In your Razor page
@page "/your-page"
@inject HttpClient _http
@inject ITADService ITADService

@code {
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await ITADService.GetAllGames();
    }

    // Optionally, you can also define a method to call the service
    private async Task CallGetAllGames()
    {
        await ITADService.GetAllGames();
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **`HttpClient` and `ITADService` Injection:**
  - Ensure that `HttpClient` and `ITADService` are injected into the Razor page.
- **`OnInitializedAsync`:**
  - Use `await` to call the `GetAllGames` method of `ITADService`.
- **Optional Method:**
  - Optionally, define a method to call the service, which can be useful if you need to call it from other parts of the page.

This approach ensures that the `ITADService` is called within an asynchronous context, which resolves the `CS0120` error.

If you still encounter issues, make sure that the `ITADService` is properly defined and that the `GetAllGames` method is correctly implemented.

