Title: How to apply a time limit to a web service call in ColdFusion?.
Body: <p>I'm working on a system that calls an external web service to obtain data. It appears that when something fails in the web service, the caller is left hanging and the template never ends.</p>
<p>There is a CFSETTING REQUESTTIMEOUT in the calling template, but it does not seem to be applied to the web service call. The calling code uses CFSCRIPT and I am uncomfortable with the syntax. Can someone advise me how to apply a timeout to the following code?</p>
<pre><code>ws = CreateObject(&quot;webservice&quot;, &quot;http://#trim(arguments.RemoteSite)#&quot;,{wsversion=&quot;2&quot;});
ret = ws.GetJData(&quot;#arguments.clubid#&quot;, #datepart('yyyy',arguments.StartDate)#, #datepart('m',arguments.StartDate)#);
</code></pre>

Answers:
None. To apply a timeout to the web service call, you can use the <cfhttp> tag instead of <cfscript> to make the web service call. Here's an example of how you can do this:

<pre><code>&lt;cfhttp url=&quot;http://#trim(arguments.RemoteSite)#&quot; method=&quot;GET&quot; timeout=&quot;60&quot; result=&quot;httpResponse&quot;&gt;
    &lt;cfhttpparam name=&quot;clubid&quot; value=&quot;#arguments.clubid#&quot; type=&quot;formfield&quot;&gt;
    &lt;cfhttpparam name=&quot;StartDate&quot; value=&quot;#datepart('yyyy',arguments.StartDate)#&quot; type=&quot;formfield&quot;&gt;
&lt;/cfhttp&gt;

&lt;cfset ret = httpResponse.filecontent&gt;
</code></pre>

This code uses the <cfhttp> tag to make a GET request to the web service URL. The timeout attribute specifies the timeout in seconds. The result attribute is used to store the response from the web service call in the httpResponse variable. Finally, the filecontent attribute of the httpResponse variable is used to store the response from the web service call in the ret variable. This way, the web service call will be timed out after 60 seconds if it is not completed.

