Title: Azure communication service email sending error.
Body: <p>I created a communication service in azure to send mail. Then I added a verified custom domain. However, when I send an email, I get an error like this;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>RestError: The specified sender domain has not been linked.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I am able to send successfully with azure managed domain mail.</p>
<p>Here is my code:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code> const connectionString = `endpoint=https://*******`;
    const client = new EmailClient(connectionString);

    const emailMessage = {
        sender: &quot;noreply@****.com&quot;,
        content: {
            subject: &quot;This is the subject&quot;,
            plainText: &quot;This is the body&quot;,
        },
        recipients: {
            to: [
                {
                    email: &quot;*****&quot;,
                    displayName: &quot;Test test&quot;,
                },
            ],
        },
    };

    const message = await client.send(emailMessage);
</code></pre>
<p>How can I solve this problem ?</p>

Answers:
To send an email from Symfony without running the consume command, you can use the <code>SendEmailMessage</code> class and its <code>send()</code> method. This method allows you to send an email directly without using the message queue. Here's an example of how to use it:

<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$email = (new Email())
    -&gt;from('from@gmail.com')
    -&gt;to('go@gmail.com')
    -&gt;subject('Here is my subject')
    -&gt;html('&lt;p&gt;Here is the content&lt;/p&gt;');

$sendEmailMessage = new SendEmailMessage($email);
$mailer-&gt;send($sendEmailMessage);
</code></pre>

In this example, we create a new <code>SendEmailMessage</code> object and pass it the <code>Email</code> object that we want to send. Then, we call the <code>send()</code> method on the mailer object to send the email.

Note that you don't need to use the consume command to send an email using the <code>SendEmailMessage</code> class. The <code>send()</code> method will automatically send the email using the configured mailer transport.
